# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# rulesync — source of truth is rulesync.jsonc + rulesync.lock (committed).
# Regenerate skills with:
#   npx rulesync install && npx rulesync generate --targets claudecode --features skills
.claude/skills/*
.rulesync/

# ...except the vendored productivity skills. rulesync keys its lockfile by repo
# slug alone, so it can only track one path per upstream repo — we point it at
# mattpocock/skills:skills/engineering, and these five (from skills/productivity)
# are committed by hand. /grill-with-docs delegates to /grilling, so without them
# it is a no-op. Update by re-copying from upstream; they have no dependencies.
!.claude/skills/grill-me/
!.claude/skills/grilling/
!.claude/skills/handoff/
!.claude/skills/teach/
!.claude/skills/writing-great-skills/
